00:01:36,448 --> 00:01:39,048
Toly can talk for hours about FPS and frames,

31
00:01:39,108 --> 00:01:41,268
About CPU, memory, Windows and games.

32
00:01:41,288 --> 00:01:43,548
Then he’ll ask so innocent, like: “Dad, tell me why

33
00:01:43,588 --> 00:01:45,888
People on the internet are often so unkind?”

34
00:01:45,908 --> 00:01:48,289
Tolik’s a good kid, you can see it in his eyes,

35
00:01:48,529 --> 00:01:50,569
Not the type who tries to act like tough guys.

36
00:01:50,589 --> 00:01:52,749
He can disappear for days inside the screen,

37
00:01:52,769 --> 00:01:55,109
But inside he’s still that stubborn teen.

38
00:01:55,129 --> 00:01:57,429
“Time to go outside!” - sounds like a final boss,

39
00:01:57,449 --> 00:01:59,710
Tosik looks so sad, like the screen went dark.

40
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:02,190
But five minutes later - Talyan’s on the run,

41
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:04,630
Bringing juice and a croissant, having fun.

42
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:08,810
And even if school feels like a boss fight,

43
